Olloc is a [[Zong|Zongic]]-[[Balboa|Balboan]] soup dish consisting of {{w|broth}}, {{w|rice noodles}}, {{w|herbs}}, and {{w|meat}} -- usually {{w|beef}} (''olloc vadella''), sometimes {{w|chicken}} (''olloc pollastre''). Olloc is a popular food in Balboa, primarily the city of [[Sant Cristòfor]], where it was invented during the [[Zong occupation of Sant Cristòfor]] period from 1899-1947. The dish was created from a fusion from older noodle soups dishes that originated in the Jade Peninsula and the demand for beef dishes of the local Balboa population.

== History ==
The first serving of Olloc can be traced to ''Xef Cafe'' in [[San Cristofor]], the restaurant was known for pork stews but started serving beef and offal based rice noodle dishes. The word olloc comes from a zongic shortening of ''olla de foc'', or pot of fire.

Olloc in the modern day is enjoyed worldwide.

